    {
      "text": "A connection formula between the Ramanujan function and the q -Airy function — We show a connection formula between two diﬀerent q-Airy func- tions.\n\n**A connection formula between the Ramanujan function and the q -Airy function**\n\n*Takeshi MORITA‡*\n\n12 pp, 11 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We show a connection formula between two diﬀerent q-Airy func- tions. One is called the Ramanujan function which appears in Ra- manujan’s ”Lost notebook”. Another one is called the q-Airy function that obtained in the study of the second q-Painlev´e equation. We use the q-Borel transformation and the q-Laplace transformation following C. Zhang to obtain the connection formula.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Standard notations; 3 Two types of the q-analogue of the Airy func; 3.1 The Ramanujan function Aq(x); 3.2 The q-Airy function Aiq(x); 3.3 Shearing transformations; 3.4 The q-Airy equation around the infinity; 4 The q-Borel transformation, the q-Laplace tr; 4.1 The q-Borel transformation and the q-Lapla; 4.2 The connection formula of the q-Airy funct",
